Planning That Gives Importance to Open Spaces
Residential planning is not limited to the apartment interiors. The spaces between buildings, landscaped areas and recreational zones can influence how residents experience a community.

CRC Sublimis includes a variety of planned outdoor areas, including a peace lawn, seating garden, pebble garden, youth garden, celebration lawn and tree grove. The site plan also includes pathways, pergolas, landscaped areas and dedicated recreational spaces.

This approach provides residents with different settings for recreation, relaxation and community activities. The development also includes individual drop-off zones for the towers and designated parking and access areas as part of the site layout.

Amenities for Different Age Groups
A residential community becomes more functional when its facilities cater to different interests and age groups. CRC Sublimis includes both outdoor and indoor amenities as part of its overall planning.

Outdoor facilities listed by CRC include a swimming pool and kids’ pool, mini golf, half basketball court, tennis court, party lawn, amphitheatre, children’s play area, elderly park and fitness court. These facilities provide options for exercise, recreation and leisure without requiring residents to leave the community for every activity.

The project also includes indoor facilities such as a poolside library, table tennis and billiards, squash, an indoor badminton and multipurpose hall, indoor games, a café and lounge, and a dance and yoga room.

Rather than focusing on one type of recreation, the amenity mix provides different spaces that can accommodate varied routines and interests.

