Why Floor Plans Deserve Careful Attention
Two apartments with similar advertised areas can feel very different once the internal layout is considered. Room dimensions, passage space, balcony placement, kitchen arrangement and storage can all affect how comfortably a home works for a particular family.

CRC Sublimis provides several configurations, which gives prospective buyers an opportunity to compare different layouts. The 2 BHK + Study option, for example, provides an additional room that may be useful as a study, work area or flexible family space, depending on the household’s needs.

The 3 BHK configurations provide additional room capacity, while the listed ground-floor option includes a private garden. Buyers should compare these layouts based on how they intend to use each space rather than selecting a configuration solely by its total area.

Checking the Project Before Making a Decision
A property visit remains an important part of the home-buying process. Photographs and floor plans can provide useful information, but they do not fully communicate the scale of the buildings, the surrounding environment or the experience of moving through the development.

Prospective buyers should review the applicable project documentation, confirm the latest specifications and check the relevant RERA information. CRC Sublimis is listed with UP RERA under registration number UPRERAPRJ15180.

It is also worth comparing the actual apartment layout with the documents provided for the specific unit. Any applicable charges, specifications, maintenance arrangements and other contractual details should be clarified with the authorised representatives before proceeding.

